<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 232)</h2>
<p><b>The watch folder now asks Kitsu, not just the filesystem.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>A delivery named <code>SHOT_vNNN</code> landing in a watched folder is checked against the tracker: if that version's preview already exists in Kitsu, the render is done by definition — it ingests <b>immediately</b>, instead of waiting for the file to go quiet. (In testing: 6 seconds, against a 2-minute quiet window.)</li>
<li>Tracker-confirmed deliveries arrive <b>carrying their Kitsu task</b> — a shot that walked in through the watch folder can be published straight back with File → Publish Review to Kitsu, notes, marked frames and all.</li>
<li>Everything stays fail-open: no Kitsu project set, shot unknown, tracker unreachable — the done-marker and quiet-file rules work exactly as before.</li>
<li>Uses the project remembered by the Review List panel; nothing new to configure.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
